 "notes": "Strip c: x 3960-5560 plus overlap 3660-5860, full height. Washington printed 'WASHINGTON' (suffix not seen in this strip). Monroe Avenue / Ashland Avenue is a skewed junction at Ashland's bend (Ashland E-W to the west, NE-SW to the north-east, Monroe crossing NW-SE); centre approximate (~15 px). Thin lines drawn along some street centres (e.g. Monroe, Burwood, Shanmoor) taken as boundary/centre lines, not streets. Not streets: Lafayette-side railroad along the NW plate edge, the railroad paralleling Forest Avenue, Duck Creek, the grey/pink/green boundary bands, the coal-bin siding at the bottom. Large spaced lettering 'PARK', 'ANNA B.', 'N...S', 'B O', 'M ... E' etc. is subdivision lettering. Burwood south of Morton continues SSE to a dead end at Duck Creek (pick 'Burwood Avenue' end). Cameron Avenue's diagonal leg from the bend at x~4080 is labelled only 'AVE.'; taken as Cameron."
